description:
All code cited lives in the jr_be repo (~/code/EloRated/jr_be) unless noted.

The legacy whole-video analyzer is still auto-triggered on 'ready' and it races (and beats) the chunked pipeline, permanently preventing the chunked path from running.

Evidence:
- `supabase/functions/video-webhook/index.ts:288-291` fires the legacy whole-video analyzer whenever the status becomes 'ready':
  ```
  if (status === "ready") {
    // Auto-trigger analysis for ready videos
    // In production, this could be gated by a feature flag or user preference
    analysisTriggered = await triggerAnalysis(video_id);
  }
  ```
- That runs in the same handler that flips `match_videos.status` to 'ready'. The same status flip also fires the pg_net slice POST via the `trg_match_videos_request_slice_update` trigger, so two dispatches race.
- `video-analyze` (the legacy path) sets `status='analyzing'` synchronously and almost always wins that race.
- By the time the slicer's `/slice` request lands, the row is no longer 'ready', so the worker bails at `workers/video-slicer/src/main.js:780-784`:
  ```
  if (existing.status !== "ready") {
    log("info", "slice skipped: status not ready", { video_id: videoId, status: existing.status });
    jsonReply(res, 200, { skipped: true, reason: `status=${existing.status}` });
    return;
  }
  ```
- Recovery is impossible: the `request-pending-video-slices` cron sweep only re-dispatches rows with `status = 'ready'`, and the row is now 'analyzing'. The chunked pipeline never runs for that video.

Fix shape: delete the `triggerAnalysis(video_id)` call at `supabase/functions/video-webhook/index.ts:288-291`, or put it behind an explicit feature flag that is OFF by default (the chunked pipeline is the supported path per specs/013-chunked-video-pipeline). If the legacy `video-analyze` function is being retired, note that in the issue that removes it; if it is retained for manual re-analysis, leave it callable but not auto-triggered.

Found by the queries.ts audit for jits-icei.5. This is a different shape from the rest of the audit and is worth fixing on its own.

packages/shared/src/api/queries.ts, getArenaData:

    const { data, error } = await supabase.rpc('get_arena_data', { p_limit: limit });
    if (error) console.error('getArenaData:', error);
    return data as unknown as ArenaData;

The error is logged and then ignored, and data (null on failure) is cast straight to ArenaData. The caller is handed null with a non-nullable type, so the first property access throws a TypeError. Every other aggregate read in the file at least returns a safe empty value; this one returns a lie the type system actively hides.

Compare getDashboardSummary two functions above, which throws on the same condition (if (error || !data) throw). Arena should do one of the two, not neither.

FIX SHAPE: either throw like getDashboardSummary (its caller already has an error boundary), or return Result<ArenaData>. Arena is on web and mobile, so check both call sites first. apps/web is owned by another session; coordinate.
